HST Office: oversized ribbon groups become labelled "Caption ▾" menu buttons, as in the reference suite.

Gap list G10 (owner, 15/11/2026): a group must not fall back to bare icons while the ribbon has room. Writer ▸ Bố cục
▸ Sắp xếp (18 commands) becomes Vị trí ▾, Bao quanh văn bản ▾, Tiến lên ▾, Lùi xuống ▾, Căn chỉnh ▾, Nhóm ▾, Xoay ▾
beside the labelled Ngăn dẫn hướng, Chọn and Vị trí và kích cỡ; Writer ▸ Xem lại ▸ Thay đổi becomes Chấp nhận ▾ and
Từ chối ▾ beside the labelled Trước and Tiếp; Sheets ▸ Bố trí trang ▸ Sắp xếp becomes Tiến lên ▾, Lùi xuống ▾,
Căn chỉnh ▾, Nhóm ▾, Xoay ▾ beside Chọn and Ngăn dẫn hướng; Sheets ▸ Dữ liệu ▸ Phân tích (10 statistical tests) is
one large Phân tích dữ liệu ▾; Draw ▸ Sắp xếp gets Tiến lên ▾ and Lùi xuống ▾ beside Căn chỉnh, and Xoay ▾ beside
Biến đổi ▾ (which now also holds the transform mode). Every grid keeps its id, so the adaptive ladders still apply;
the menu items take their labels and icons from their commands (Writer's wrap and anchor items reuse the labels of
its picture and shape tabs). A menu button's "hst-ribbon-description" becomes the second line of its tooltip, as
for the ribbon's tool buttons; the menu items that take their label from their command are listed in the
gla11y suppressions, as Menu HstTransform's are. The Vietnamese strings come from l10n/vi-overrides.jsonl.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
---
--- a/vcl/source/window/builder.cxx
+++ b/vcl/source/window/builder.cxx
@@ -1390,6 +1390,18 @@
         if (!sMenu.isEmpty())
             m_pVclParserState->m_aButtonMenuMaps.emplace_back(id, sMenu);
         setupFromActionName(static_cast<Button*>(xWindow.get()), rMap, m_xFrame);
+        // HST: a ribbon menu button ("Wrap Text ▾") shows the ribbon's second tooltip line too:
+        // "hst-ribbon-description", under its label
+        const auto aDescription = rMap.find(u"hst-ribbon-description"_ustr);
+        if (aDescription != rMap.end())
+        {
+            const auto aLabel = rMap.find(u"label"_ustr);
+            const OUString sLabel = aLabel == rMap.end() ? OUString() : aLabel->second.replaceAll("~", "");
+            if (!aDescription->second.isEmpty())
+                xWindow->SetQuickHelpText(sLabel.isEmpty() ? aDescription->second
+                                                           : sLabel + "\n" + aDescription->second);
+            rMap.erase(aDescription);
+        }
     }
     else if (name == "sfxlo-PriorityMergedHBox")
     {
